              "type": "blob_dialog",
              "content": "Momentum is conserved in every collision. Kinetic energy is not.",
              "metadata": {
                "version": 1,
                "lines": [
                  {
                    "id": "l1",
                    "text": "Momentum is conserved in every collision. Kinetic energy is not.",
                    "mood": "thinking",
                    "cta": "Never?"
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "l2",
                    "text": "Only in an elastic collision. In an inelastic one, energy goes into heat and deformation.",
                    "mood": "happy",
                    "cta": "So how do I choose?"
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "l3",
                    "text": "Start with momentum every time. Bring in energy only when the question says elastic.",
                    "mood": "cheer",
                    "cta": "Good rule"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "al-2-2",
              "type": "formula",
              "content": "m_1u_1 + m_2u_2 = m_1v_1 + m_2v_2"
            },
            {
              "id": "al-2-3",
              "type": "text",
              "content": "**Impulse** is the same idea in another form: force multiplied by contact time equals the change in momentum. That is why a longer contact time means a gentler force, and why crumple zones exist."
            }
          ],
          "evaluateBlocks": [
