          "learnBlocks": [
            {
              "id": "al-6-1",
              "type": "blob_dialog",
              "content": "By this point you have several models, and the exam skill is choosing between them.",
              "metadata": {
                "version": 1,
                "lines": [
                  {
                    "id": "l1",
                    "text": "By this point you have several models, and the exam skill is choosing between them.",
                    "mood": "thinking",
                    "cta": "How do I choose?"
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "l2",
                    "text": "Ask what is steady and what is changing. Steady current means Ohm's law; a changing one means the capacitor is involved.",
                    "mood": "happy",
                    "cta": "And mechanics?"
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "l3",
                    "text": "Same question. Constant acceleration allows the equations of motion. Otherwise think in energy or momentum.",
                    "mood": "cheer",
                    "cta": "That is the map"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "al-6-2",
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A quick sort:\n\n- **Steady circuit** with fixed resistances: Ohm's law and power.\n- **Changing circuit** with a capacitor: charge, time constant, exponential behaviour.\n- **Constant acceleration**: the equations of motion.\n- **Collision or sudden force**: momentum and impulse.\n- **Neither, but energy is trackable**: work and energy conservation."
            },
            {
              "id": "al-6-3",
              "type": "callout",
              "content": "Write down which model you chose and why. Examiners give credit for a stated valid approach even when the arithmetic goes wrong."
            }
          ],
          "evaluateBlocks": [
            {
              "id": "al-eb-6-1",
              "type": "drag_drop",
              "question": "Match each situation to the model that fits it.",
              "correctAnswer": "slot-charging:capacitor,slot-collision:momentum,slot-steady:ohm",
              "explanation": "Sorting by what is steady and what is changing points at the right model before any algebra starts.",
              "metadata": {
                "version": 1,
                "items": [
                  {
                    "id": "ohm",
                    "label": "Ohm's law and power"
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "capacitor",
                    "label": "Capacitor charge and time constant"
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "momentum",
                    "label": "Momentum and impulse"
                  }
                ],
                "slots": [
                  {
                    "id": "slot-steady",
                    "label": "A lamp on a steady supply"
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "slot-charging",
                    "label": "A circuit switched on with a capacitor in it"
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "slot-collision",
                    "label": "Two trolleys colliding on a track"
                  }
                ]
              }
